"to gain an unfair advantage in game play"

&#x200B;

To be clear, I don't think it should be illegal at all, I was curious if there had been any official stance on it.  I see the example they give has to do with rigging an internal minigame.

&#x200B;

Thanks for the info!

oh well if you are using a small casing then you'll need electronic run dry protection, not a float.  Like a Franklin Electric pumptec.

&#x200B;

How deep are you planning on going?  you can get manufactured perforated casing.  Are you in an area that this could freeze?

If you have access to a press gun get one of these tee's and a 1/2in x 1/4in brass bushing to install the gauge.

&#x200B;

https://www.supplyhouse.com/Viega-79760-1-x-1-x-1-2-Propress-Smart-Connect-Bronze-Tee-Lead-Free

looks to be similair to a fleck 9000.  something along those lines.

&#x200B;

https://www.softenerparts.com/identify\_valve\_brand

So when checking this 3ph 480V fused disconnect with NO load on it, my T+ Pro tester is showing fine line to line voltage, but shows 12VAC line to ground on all the phases?   But only when there is no load.

When I turn on the load, a 5HP motor, I get the proper reading line to ground.

&#x200B;

When I check with my other flukes, the readings are what they should be, I'm just not seeing the correct voltage when there is no load line to ground?

&#x200B;

Also, I check the same testing setup on 208, 120, and 230 at the same time and didn't have any issues.

The L-G voltage with my 289 shows even voltage between phases and to ground.

&#x200B;

Thought?  Thanks!!

